<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I9369f8f42508c982e9a4f571ac8789d7733f8592" commit="53f689884391e06a8e99082ac6ce7a5869649e3e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mac80211: Align skbs before delivering to NSS  BUG=None TEST=build/boot on storm. Connect a station to the AP and verify if traffic is flowing after enabling NSS redirect  Change-Id: I9369f8f42508c982e9a4f571ac8789d7733f8592 Signed-off-by: Vivek Natarajan &lt;nataraja@codeaurora.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;arnagara@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/310165 Commit-Ready: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="310165" owner_email="arnagara@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/65/310165/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="If3572b9c2ef065f9de3996bd420d9d5220041672" commit="6d6e48c5aebd7134186408bffc55caa31d9160ff" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mac80211: Fix data stall issue when sending DL traffic  With current top of tree, AP will stop sending traffic after we send heavy UDP DL traffic.  The issue is not observed when I disable NSS support from mac80211.  With these changes, AP will wait for HTT free Tx queues to send data.  BUG=none TEST=none  Change-Id: If3572b9c2ef065f9de3996bd420d9d5220041672 Signed-off-by: Anilkumar kolli &lt;akolli@codeaurora.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;arnagara@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/310166 Commit-Ready: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="310166" owner_email="arnagara@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/66/310166/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I1f30b2267a420ae454e4fc7510a134376d114a80" commit="a8057cc38c2b315cf459a09b506f054da411b784" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mac80211: add tx frames to pending list when queues are stopped  Packets from NSS are dropped when queues are stopped by driver due to out of resources. Dropping TCP packets is affecting throughput on downlink direction. Hence queue up the frames into pending list until it is woken up by driver. Since NSS driver does not support net device pause and unpause, pending queue depth is maintained to avoid memory overload. This change is improving TCP DL by 10 Mbps.  BUG=none TEST=none  Change-Id: I1f30b2267a420ae454e4fc7510a134376d114a80 Signed-off-by: Rajkumar Manoharan &lt;rmanohar@codeaurora.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;arnagara@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/310167 Commit-Ready: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kishan Kunduru &lt;kkunduru@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="310167" owner_email="arnagara@codeaurora.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/67/310167/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Iff024372323deb4cd89d1f3ca3d139d0b60fd877" commit="33551f1d420a871bb156b9f9332dc2aca2f63ea3" commit_message="FROMLIST: usb: dwc2: host: Get aligned DMA in a more supported way  All other host controllers who want aligned buffers for DMA do it a certain way.  Let's do that too instead of working behind the USB core's back.  This makes our interrupt handler not take forever and also rips out a lot of code, simplifying things a bunch.  This also has the side effect of removing the 65535 max transfer size limit.  NOTE: The actual code to allocate the aligned buffers is ripped almost completely from the tegra EHCI driver.  At some point in the future we may want to add this functionality to the USB core to share more code everywhere.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46623 TEST=Audio is better; other stuff still works  Change-Id: Iff024372323deb4cd89d1f3ca3d139d0b60fd877 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Heiko Stuebner &lt;heiko@sntech.de&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/7574391/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/310584 " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="310584" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/84/310584/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3eca02641e51ed52fc0fee50de1f0fd1a7adb6e3" commit="b62edb3fcfce799922b7a750ee68f8c4b7605013" commit_message="quipper: PerfOptionParser: Fix a past-the-end bug for value arguments  If a value argument is at the end of the vector, args_iter would get incremented twice. Since the loop condition is an equality comparison with the end iterator, the for loop could go beyond the bounds of the vector.  Check for being at the end after skipping over an argument value, and add some test cases.  TEST=Added unit test BUG=chromium:537464  Change-Id: I3eca02641e51ed52fc0fee50de1f0fd1a7adb6e3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311834 Commit-Ready: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Sharp &lt;dhsharp@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Emma Rapati &lt;rapati@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="311834" owner_email="dhsharp@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/34/311834/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4d49ae503708350dbb3c617243d70e2b257817f4" commit="77ad34f62509baa0b1ba446a760008db046b18e7" commit_message="[Autotest] Add /var/log/messages checking to bluetooth_AdapterSanity  As part of the test, check /var/log/messages for any suspicious kernel errors.  Fail test if found.  Ignore some known issues.  BUG=chromium:536123 TEST=ran across many devices  Change-Id: I4d49ae503708350dbb3c617243d70e2b257817f4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311830 Commit-Ready: Katherine Threlkeld &lt;kathrelkeld@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Katherine Threlkeld &lt;kathrelkeld@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tien Chang &lt;tienchang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="311830" owner_email="kathrelkeld@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/30/311830/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I04ec026472b85d4bcd841e6bf9b645996156bf2a" commit="7c4de874ed65b89cf6c80efae475260a7c88e7b4" commit_message="login: thaw renderers before killing processes  Chrome renderers are frozen in some circumstances, such as during dark resume. If Chrome crashes during this time, the renderers will be left in the freezer, and we won't be able to kill them when we try to restart the UI. This leaves renderers orphaned.  BUG=chromium:551116 TEST=run as root:   # echo FROZEN &gt; \     /sys/fs/cgroup/freezer/chrome_renderers/to_be_frozen/freezer.state   # ps aux | grep renderer   # restart ui   # ps aux | grep renderer   and make sure the first set of renderers is not hanging around.  Change-Id: I04ec026472b85d4bcd841e6bf9b645996156bf2a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311309 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="311309" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/09/311309/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibed423f4a8a582dd775723556c3b96f000bc535d" commit="0cc2215bf792ad2396d0a104ae057e08c1db003d" commit_message="power_LoadTest: log memory bandwidth  Dumps human-readable memory bandwidth logs into the .DEBUG file. This might be useful for debugging power issues since these values can act as a proxy for processor activity.  BUG=None TEST=run power_LoadTest.fast with log_mem_bandwidth=True and inspect   DEBUG logs  Change-Id: Ibed423f4a8a582dd775723556c3b96f000bc535d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/252271 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="252271" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/71/252271/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="If9e3d719ad0935d25d575aa7054ebbcade2d4236" commit="a48bedb414f0f68d49992ae487f9632b9544c008" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mmc: sdhci-tegra: Warn on register accesses while clock gated  If a Tegra210 SDHCI register is accessed while the core is clock gated, it will hang the bus, causing a watchdog reset.  We've seen a few reports of watchdog resets immediately following SD bus errors, leading to speculation that there might be an improper register access somewhere. Add a few new checks that will log a warning + backtrace if this happens.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45478 TEST=manual  Change-Id: If9e3d719ad0935d25d575aa7054ebbcade2d4236 Signed-off-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311856 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="311856" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/56/311856/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5e66eb94e31299b27ce029b7f7ce6ba0a7fb6816" commit="8f88d8859d001f82812a3fe4b2487eb14ff2d5ce" commit_message="console: Add support for using EC-3PO console.  This commit introduces a new CONFIG_* option.  To utilise the experimental console, simply define the following config option in the board's board.h file.       #define CONFIG_EXPERIMENTAL_CONSOLE  This is a temporary option which allows the EC console to be work with the EC-3PO interactive console interface.  When this option is enabled, the EC expects commands to packed in a particular format.  This is for command integrity and allows the interpreter to perform automatic command retrying in the event that a character is dropped from the sent command.  It also removes a lot of the console editing methods since they are now being served by EC-3PO.  Once the EC-3PO interpreter is pulled into servod, we can enable this feature by default and the config option can go away.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46054 BRANCH=None TEST=make -j buildall tests TEST=Enable CONFIG_EXPERIMENTAL_CONSOLE on GLaDOS; Flash EC and verify that console works via the EC-3PO interactive console interface. TEST=Build and flash on GLaDOS and verify normal console operation on standard EC UART.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:308615  Change-Id: I5e66eb94e31299b27ce029b7f7ce6ba0a7fb6816 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309991 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309991" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/91/309991/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I762f6f5a0a34cb52d86b1de5e95f7c53316b29eb" commit="8b2ebaa514165f56e08615b627703ad6147e31ab" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iio: cros_ec: Move core attributes in sensors_core.  Attributes frequency and sampling_frequency are processed identically for all sensors. Move the code in cros_ec_sensors_core.  BUG=b:25425420 TEST=CTS Sensor Tests still works.  Change-Id: I762f6f5a0a34cb52d86b1de5e95f7c53316b29eb Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311374 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="311374" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/74/311374/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idebb3247b55465f1fbf35a33dff2f00968b8f4ce" commit="d6bf1a0fdba26bc2f745685b140069a2c6164792" commit_message="common: port80: Add items to .bss.slow.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46056 BUG=chrome-os-partner:46063 BRANCH=None TEST=Enable CONFIG_REPLACE_LOADER_WITH_BSS_SLOW on GLaDOS.  Build, flash, and verify AP and EC boot.  Suspend/Resume and verify that port80 data is in the history. TEST='sysjump rw' suspend/resume nad verify that new port80 writes are present in the history. TEST=make -j buildall tests.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:311209  Change-Id: Idebb3247b55465f1fbf35a33dff2f00968b8f4ce Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311365 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="311365" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/65/311365/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7c0e8f50fb786d62e4fe13ea19ddce1dba116408" commit="ff7358635e3cc170c27fb2b76e8cee5b78248190" commit_message="Add initial dcrypto AES implementation.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:43025,chrome-os-partner:47524 TEST=none Change-Id: I7c0e8f50fb786d62e4fe13ea19ddce1dba116408 Signed-off-by: nagendra modadugu &lt;ngm@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309873 Commit-Ready: Nagendra Modadugu &lt;ngm@google.com&gt; Commit-Ready: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nagendra Modadugu &lt;ngm@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309873" owner_email="ngm@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/73/309873/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7629.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>